SEG = "COD"
CAT = "fqCode"
Q = [
    ("How many principles does the National Firearms Safety Code list?",
     "16", ["7", "10", "12"],
     "The National Firearms Safety Code, produced by the Commonwealth Attorney-General's Department, lists 16 principles, from treating every firearm as if it is loaded to disposing of unwanted firearms lawfully."),
    ("The Code warns against which habit when handling a firearm?",
     "Daydreaming", ["Wearing shooting gloves", "Using a carry sling", "Cleaning it after use"],
     "The Code says do not develop bad habits: concentrate on the task at hand and do not daydream when handling firearms."),
    ("Under the National Firearms Safety Code, you should pass or accept a firearm only when it is:",
     "Open and unloaded", ["Closed with the safety on", "Cased with the bolt in", "Loaded but uncocked"],
     "The Code says only accept or pass a firearm if the breech is open and all ammunition has been removed."),
    ("Before handing a firearm to someone, you should:",
     "Open it and check the breech", ["Close the bolt on an empty chamber", "Put the safety on and hand it over", "Take the sling off the firearm"],
     "The Code lists pointing the muzzle in a safe direction, opening the bolt or action, checking the breech is empty and checking the magazine is removed and empty."),
    ("If you do not know how to open a particular firearm, the Code says to:",
     "Leave it alone", ["Try the trigger gently", "Work every lever until it opens", "Point it down and shake it"],
     "The Code says plainly: if you do not know how to open a firearm, leave it alone."),
    ("The Code names which of these as a danger time when a firearm may fire without warning?",
     "Cocking a loaded firearm", ["Cleaning an empty firearm", "Carrying a cased firearm", "Storing a firearm in a safe"],
     "The Code says special care is needed when closing, cocking, taking off the safety catch, uncocking or opening a loaded firearm, and when unloading live rounds with the action."),
    ("According to the National Firearms Safety Code, a safe direction:",
     "Depends on where you are", ["Is always straight up", "Is always at the ground", "Is always to your left side"],
     "The Code says a safe direction depends on where you are and what you are doing, and reminds shooters that bullets can pass through walls, ceilings and car doors."),
    ("The Code reminds shooters that a bullet can kill even after passing through:",
     "A wall or a car door", ["A thick hedge only", "A shooter's own hand", "A closed steel safe door"],
     "The Code warns that bullets can kill having passed through a wall, a ceiling or a car door, so pointing a firearm at a wall or floor is not automatically safe."),
    ("The Code's explanation of principle 9 says firearm safety begins:",
     "At home", ["At the range", "In the field", "At the dealer"],
     "Under principle 9, never allow unauthorised access, the Code says firearm safety begins at home: storage of firearms and ammunition is the owner's responsibility."),
    ("Under the Code, you must never point a firearm at or near another person:",
     "Whether loaded or not", ["Unless it is unloaded", "Unless the safety is on", "Unless the bolt is out"],
     "Principle 4 says never point a firearm at or near another person, and the Code adds: loaded or unloaded, always point the muzzle in a safe direction."),
    ("The National Firearms Safety Code says you should load a firearm only when:",
     "You are ready to shoot", ["You leave the vehicle", "You reach the property gate", "You first see game"],
     "Principle 5 says never load a firearm until you are ready to shoot. In the field it is carried unloaded with the action open until you are in your shooting area."),
    ("The Code says it is not safe to have your finger inside the trigger guard until:",
     "The moment before you fire", ["You first see the target", "You take the safety off", "You leave the vehicle"],
     "The Code says it is not safe practice to have your finger on the trigger or inside the trigger guard until the moment before you are ready to fire at your target."),
    ("What does the National Firearms Safety Code say about safety catches?",
     "Never rely on them alone", ["They make a gun unloaded", "They suit fence crossings", "They replace unloading"],
     "The Code says not to rely solely on safety catches: they are mechanical devices that may fail to engage properly or be knocked off, and only supplement safe handling."),
    ("With the safety catch in the OFF or FIRE position:",
     "Pulling the trigger fires it", ["The firearm cannot fire", "The bolt cannot be opened", "The magazine is locked in"],
     "The Code explains the two positions: ON or SAFE restricts the firearm from firing, and OFF or FIRE lets it discharge when the trigger is pulled."),
    ("Most firearms show the safety catch position with:",
     "Stamped marks or coloured dots", ["A small warning light", "A click sound when it moves", "A paper tag on the stock"],
     "The Code says most firearms have markings stamped into the metalwork or coloured dots to show the current status of the safety catch."),
    ("When you finish shooting, the National Firearms Safety Code's order is:",
     "Magazine out, unload, check", ["Check chamber, unload, magazine out", "Safety on, case it, unload at home", "Unload, case it, magazine out later"],
     "Principle 7 says to remove the magazine if fitted, unload, and then check that the chamber is empty."),
    ("The Code treats a firearm as still loaded if:",
     "Its loose magazine holds a round", ["The safety catch is on", "Its bolt is fully closed", "It was fired in the last hour"],
     "The Code says your firearm is loaded if there is a live round in the chamber, or if the magazine still contains a live round even when it is not attached to the firearm."),
    ("If you take a medicine labelled as affecting your ability to drive, the Code says you should:",
     "Not go shooting", ["Shoot from a rest only", "Shoot with a partner", "Halve your dose first"],
     "The Code says do not shoot if you are on medication identified as affecting your ability to drive or operate machinery, and ask your doctor if in doubt."),
    ("The National Firearms Safety Code says you should not drink alcohol until:",
     "Your firearm is put away", ["Your last shot is fired", "You return to your vehicle", "The sun has gone down"],
     "The Code says never take alcohol or drugs before you go shooting, while you are shooting, or until your firearm has been put away safely."),
    ("The Code says you should refuse to shoot with someone who:",
     "Has been drinking alcohol", ["Owns a different calibre", "Shoots left-handed", "Is new to your shooting club"],
     "Principle 12 says never mix shooting with alcohol or drugs, and the Code advises refusing to shoot with others who are, or have been, drinking or taking drugs."),
    ("If you suspect your firearm is not in safe working order, the Code says to:",
     "Take it to a gunsmith", ["Fix it yourself at home", "Keep using it carefully", "Swap parts from another gun"],
     "The Code says it is dangerous to use a firearm not in safe working order, not to attempt your own repairs, and to have a reputable gunsmith inspect and repair it."),
    ("Who does the Code say should adjust a firearm's trigger?",
     "A qualified gunsmith", ["The owner with a spanner", "Any experienced club member", "The dealer's sales staff"],
     "The Code says trigger adjustments should only be carried out by a competent person, preferably a qualified gunsmith, because trigger pull is vital for safety."),
    ("The Code warns against exchanging bolts or bolt heads between firearms because:",
     "A gunsmith should fit them", ["It voids the licence", "It changes the category", "It wears out the barrel"],
     "The Code warns: do not exchange bolts, bolt heads or other action parts; these should be fitted by a gunsmith."),
    ("Principle 2 of the National Firearms Safety Code is:",
     "Your firearm is your responsibility", ["Your club is responsible for it", "Your dealer must check your gun", "The range officer is in charge"],
     "Principle 2 says your firearm is your responsibility: you are both legally and morally responsible for it under all circumstances."),
    ("The Code says every member of a firearm owner's family should know:",
     "Why it must not be touched", ["How to load it quickly", "Where the safe key is kept", "How to clean the barrel"],
     "The Code says to make sure all family members know what a firearm is, its capacity to kill or injure and why it should not be touched."),
    ("The National Firearms Safety Code says your firearms should be accessed only:",
     "When you are present", ["When a neighbour checks", "When the safe is open", "When guests ask to see"],
     "Principle 9 says never allow unauthorised access, and the Code adds that your firearms should only be accessed when you are present to ensure safe handling."),
    ("A companion keeps swinging a loaded rifle towards the group. Under the Code, you should:",
     "Refuse to shoot with them", ["Walk in front of them", "Ignore it and keep hunting", "Take their ammunition quietly"],
     "The Code says to encourage safe handling and to refuse to shoot with a person who does not have safe firearm practices."),
    ("The National Firearms Safety Code says that almost every firearm 'accident' involves:",
     "A breach of the Code", ["A faulty firearm", "Bad weather in the field", "Faulty factory ammunition"],
     "The Code says there are few true firearm accidents: in almost every case at least one principle of the National Firearms Safety Code has been breached."),
    ("When a firearm is not being used, the Code says to:",
     "Remove every round", ["Leave one round chambered", "Keep the magazine fitted", "Keep it cocked for safety"],
     "The Code says never leave firearms loaded, and to unload and remove all rounds or cartridges from the breech or magazine when you are not using it."),
    ("The Code says an old shotgun that may predate modern smokeless powders should be:",
     "Inspected by an expert", ["Fired with light loads", "Cleaned and used as normal", "Fired from the hip"],
     "The Code warns that many old shotguns were not made for modern smokeless powders and may explode with the wrong ammunition, so all should be inspected by an expert."),
    ("Why do shotguns with exposed hammers need extra care?",
     "Hammers can catch and fire", ["They cannot be unloaded", "They have no safety catch", "They need black powder only"],
     "The Code warns that exposed hammers may catch on clothing or other objects and fire accidentally, so these shotguns need extra care."),
    ("Why does the Code say handguns need extra care with muzzle direction?",
     "The short barrel swings easily", ["They have no trigger guard", "They cannot be fully unloaded", "They fire only one shot"],
     "The Code says great care is needed with handguns because the shorter barrel needs more concentration to keep it pointed in a safe direction."),
]
